{#
    All categories — the store's own categories as a row of round tiles.

    Ported from Nova's block of the same name and restyled to 2026: the
    heading is .block__title (which draws the primary accent bar) rather than
    Nova's .block-head, and the tiles use this theme's border/radius tokens
    instead of Nova's ornamental treatment.

    Nothing is typed here. The tiles ARE the catalogue: the storefront's
    category payload already carries `image_url` (resolved server-side —
    the bare `image` beside it is a storage path and would 404) and
    `description`, so the merchant maintains this section by maintaining
    the categories, not by re-uploading pictures into the theme.

    Filled by app.js rather than Twig: a home block receives no page data,
    the sandbox exposes no categories function, and the SDK has no categories
    component — a fetch is the only way to reach them. Same shape as Nova's
    wireCategoryGrid.

    Hidden until it has something to show, so a store with no categories
    renders nothing here instead of a titled band with a gap under it.

    | Variable             | Type    | Description                     |
    | component.title      | ?string | section title                   |
    | component.subtitle   | ?string | line under the title            |
    | component.limit      | ?int    | how many categories             |
    | component.columns    | ?string | tiles per row on desktop        |
    | component.show_text  | ?bool   | render the description line     |
    | position             | int     |                                 |

    Customizer bindings — full rules in README, "Customizer annotations".
    | Element            | Tag                         |
    | h2.block__title    | data-falak-field="title"    |
    | p.block__subtitle  | data-falak-field="subtitle" |

    The grid carries no binding: it holds no merchant-typed content.
#}
{# `default` treats false as empty and would flip a switched-off toggle back
   on, so "undefined means on" has to be tested explicitly. #}
{% set show_text = component.show_text is not defined or component.show_text %}
<section class="block block--categories" id="categories-{{ position }}"
         data-category-grid
         data-limit="{{ component.limit|default(12) }}"
         data-text="{{ show_text ? '1' : '0' }}"
         hidden {{ falak_section() }}>
    <div class="container">
        {% if component.title %}
            <h2 class="block__title" data-falak-field="title" data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.title') }}">{{ component.title }}</h2>
        {% endif %}

        {% if component.subtitle %}
            <p class="block__subtitle" data-falak-field="subtitle" data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.description') }}">{{ component.subtitle }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="cat-grid" data-category-grid-list
             style="--cat-grid-columns: {{ component.columns|default('6') }}"></div>
    </div>
</section>
